/**
@mainpage RPV Security Guardian Documentation

@section intro Introduction

RPV Security Guardian is a modular security framework designed to protect
Remotely Piloted Vehicles (RPVs) and associated systems against threats such as:

- Unauthorized access
- Data tampering
- Communication interception
- Runtime anomalies

The system focuses on **real-time monitoring**, **threat detection**, and
**defensive response mechanisms**.

---

@section architecture Architecture Overview

The project is structured into several key components:

@subsection core Core Layer
Handles:
- System initialization
- Configuration
- Lifecycle management

@subsection security Security Modules
Responsible for:
- Authentication & authorization
- Encryption / decryption
- Integrity checks

@subsection monitoring Monitoring & Detection
Provides:
- Telemetry analysis
- Anomaly detection
- Event logging

@subsection communication Communication Layer
Manages:
- Secure channels
- Protocol validation
- Packet inspection

---

@section features Key Features

- Modular and extensible design
- Real-time threat detection
- Secure communication pipeline
- Lightweight footprint for embedded systems
- Easy integration with existing RPV stacks

---

@section usage Usage

1. Build the project:
@code
mkdir build && cd build
cmake ..
make
@endcode

2. Run:
@code
./rpv_guardian
@endcode

---

@section docs Documentation Guide

- @ref modules "Modules"
- @ref classes "Classes"
- @ref files "Files"

---

@section security Security Considerations

This project enforces:
- Least privilege access
- Input validation
- Secure defaults

Ensure:
- Keys are stored securely
- Debug logs are disabled in production
- Communication channels are encrypted

---

@section future Future Work

- AI-based anomaly detection
- Integration with external SIEM systems
- Hardware-backed security modules

---

@section author Author

Project maintained by contributors of RPV Security Guardian.

*/
